{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_10b",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10b_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "The extracted details included the CCE indication, patient selection criteria, sex, mean age, FER, the type of investigation modality, ... capsule type, bowel preparation regimen (including prokinetic drugs and boosters), study design, sample size, bowel cleansing quality and CCE complete transit rate (see online supplemental tables A2 and A3).",
      "reason": "A comprehensive list of variables sought is reported (participant characteristics, intervention characteristics, outcomes, study design, sample size), with further detail deferred to supplemental tables A2/A3, and FER is explicitly defined in the Methods (text_4: 'The FER refers to additional urgent colonoscopy or flexible sigmoidoscopy required after initial CCE...'). However, explicit definitions or operationalisations are not provided for most other variables (e.g., bowel cleansing quality, complete transit rate, CCE indication categories), and funding sources are not mentioned as a sought data item, so the 'listed and defined' requirement is only partially met."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10b_e2",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No assumptions made about missing or unclear study information (e.g., how unreported, ambiguous, or incompletely described data were handled or interpreted during extraction) are described anywhere in the retrieved evidence. The statements about 'unclear patient selection criteria' and 'unclear definitions of CCE indications' (text_11) relate to risk-of-bias judgements, not to assumptions made by the reviewers about missing or unclear data."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10b_e3",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The manuscript does not report using any tool to determine which data items to collect. The only cited frameworks/tools are PRISMA (reporting guideline), PROSPERO (registration), ROBIN-E (risk of bias assessment), and R packages (statistical analysis); none serves to determine data items. The extracted variables appear author-specified based on the review aims, so this conditional requirement does not apply."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 78
